{"nodes": [{"id": "quality_integration_tests_dialect_integration_tests", "label": "Dialect Integration Tests (T-1, ADR 43)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Audit finding T-1 / ADR 43. Non-H2 merge SQL was previously verified by string assertion only, so a grammar typo would fail no test; at runtime the first failing store() throws BadSqlGrammarException, the store permanently flips to the INSERT/UPDATE fallback and the broken merge is silently masked. Real containers close that gap."}, {"id": "quality_integration_tests_native_merge_dialect", "label": "Native Merge/Upsert Dialect", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-database atomic upsert: H2 MERGE INTO ... KEY, PostgreSQL INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE, MySQL/MariaDB INSERT ... ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE, Oracle MERGE INTO ... USING SELECT FROM DUAL, other databases fall back to INSERT + UPDATE."}, {"id": "quality_integration_tests_failoverstorejdbc", "label": "FailoverStoreJdbc", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "quality_integration_tests_defaultfailoverstorequeryresolver", "label": "DefaultFailoverStoreQueryResolver", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Selects the merge dialect per database (ADR 13: JDBC native merge/upsert dialect detection and runtime fallback). Adding a dialect means adding the SQL constant plus a contains() branch here."}, {"id": "quality_integration_tests_abstractdialectit", "label": "AbstractDialectIT", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Holds the shared store/merge/find/cleanByExpiry/delete round-trip scenario so a new dialect only supplies a @Container and DDL subclass, with no test logic rewritten."}, {"id": "quality_integration_tests_postgresdialectit", "label": "PostgresDialectIT", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "quality_integration_tests_mysqldialectit", "label": "MySqlDialectIT", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "quality_integration_tests_mariadbdialectit", "label": "MariaDbDialectIT", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "quality_integration_tests_testcontainers", "label": "Testcontainers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://testcontainers.com/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "quality_integration_tests_dialect_its_profile", "label": "dialect-its Maven Profile", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "*DialectIT is excluded from the default failsafe config and runs only under the dialect-its profile, which needs a Docker daemon. Testcontainers JARs stay test-scoped so the sources always compile; only container startup is gated."}, {"id": "quality_integration_tests_oracle_not_containerised", "label": "Oracle Intentionally Not Containerised", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The gvenzl/oracle-free image is ~2 GB with slow startup and licensing caveats; Oracle MERGE USING DUAL stays string-asserted because PostgreSQL + MySQL + MariaDB already cover the two distinct non-H2 merge grammars."}, {"id": "quality_integration_tests_string_assertion_only_gap", "label": "String-assertion-only Verification Gap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Asserting on the SQL string proves the constant exists, not that the grammar is valid; the defect only surfaces at runtime and is then masked by the silent fallback."}], "edges": [{"source": "quality_integration_tests_dialect_integration_tests", "target": "quality_integration_tests_dialect_its_profile", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "quality_integration_tests_dialect_integration_tests", "target": "quality_integration_tests_testcontainers", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "quality_integration_tests_dialect_integration_tests", "target": "quality_integration_tests_string_assertion_only_gap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/quality/integration-tests.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "quality_integration_tests_string_assertion_only_gap", "target": "quality_integration_tests_native_merge_dialect", "r